{
  "mn117:0.1": "Middle Discourses 117 ",
  "mn117:0.2": "The Great Forty ",
  "mn117:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn117:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn117:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn117:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn117:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn117:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn117:2.1": "“Mendicants, I will teach you noble right immersion with its vital conditions and its prerequisites. ",
  "mn117:2.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "mn117:2.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn117:2.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn117:3.1": "“And what is noble right immersion with its vital conditions and its prerequisites? ",
  "mn117:3.2": "They are: right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, and right mindfulness. ",
  "mn117:3.3": "Unification of mind with these seven factors as prerequisites ",
  "mn117:3.4": "is called noble right immersion ‘with its vital conditions’ and also ‘with its prerequisites’. ",
  "mn117:4.1": "In this context, right view comes first. ",
  "mn117:4.2": "And how does right view come first? ",
  "mn117:4.3": "When you understand wrong view as wrong view and right view as right view, that’s your right view. ",
  "mn117:5.1": "And what is wrong view? ",
  "mn117:5.2": "‘There’s no meaning in giving, sacrifice, or offerings. There’s no fruit or r